{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home","id":1375873,"title":"WoD Stuff to Watch While Home","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-20T16:59:41-07:00","id":1375873,"title":"WoD Stuff to Watch While Home","content":"So, with a lot of people stuck at home, I figured it would be worthwhile to share suggestions on stuff to watch that makes good WoD viewing. My only really criteria here is that it be stuff that's available on various streaming services - Netflix, Amazon Prime, Hulu, etc. - without requiring any additional outlay of money. <br /> <br /> I'll start with three on Amazon Prime.<br /> <br /> <b>Annihilation</b> (2018), with Natalie Portman as the leader of a team investigating a warp in reality. It's an interesting visual inspiration for landscapes that are both alien and familiar at the same time (including those of the Umbra). <br /> <br /> <b>Edge of Darkness</b> (2010), a low key outing with Mel Gibson as a father investigating the death of his daughter. I especially recommend it for Vampire and Werewolf viewing, for reasons.<br /> <br /> <b>The Decent</b> (2005), in which a group of women go caving and regret it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T00:44:21-07:00","id":1375908,"title":"","content":"Others might not agree, but I think The Pagemaster is a great Changeling story. I don't know if its on any streaming services but it could work for a high Glamour Changeling as the Pagemaster enchanting the boy in order to inspire him as he would be very high Banality beforehand. The Library being the Freehold, the Fantasy World being the Dreaming and the books being Chimera.<br /> Its cheesy but one of my favorite childhood movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:07:13-07:00","id":1375957,"title":"","content":"What We Do In The Shadows, both the 2014 movie and 2019 is a lighthearted take on Vampire the Masquerade IMO. It's gloriously goofy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T09:39:18-07:00","id":1375977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1375957#post1375957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What We Do In The Shadows, both the 2014 movie and 2019 is a lighthearted take on Vampire the Masquerade IMO. It's gloriously goofy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Season 2 of the show premieres next month!<br /> <br /> I've been looking for copies of the classic cold war nuclear scares of my childhood from the 80's, like &quot;The Day After&quot; or Threads,&quot; but I'm not seeing anything budget-friendly on any of the streaming services I currently have accounts on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T10:20:07-07:00","id":1375979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1375977#post1375977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking for copies of the classic cold war nuclear scares of my childhood from the 80's, like &quot;The Day After&quot; or Threads,&quot; but I'm not seeing anything budget-friendly on any of the streaming services I currently have accounts on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've never seen it, 1988's <b>Miracle Mile</b> is a really good one. It's currently available for rent on Amazon Prime and apparently for free if you have the PlutoTV app. (However, Pluto has ad breaks during its movies, and no search function, so actually finding something specific on it is kind of a pain.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T10:45:13-07:00","id":1375981,"title":"","content":"And a few things currently on Netflix.<br /> <br /> <b>Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr. Norrell</b> (2015), a BBC miniseries based on Susanna Clarke's excellent novel about faerie magic, wizards and fair folk during the early 19th century of Britain. If you're a Mage or Changeling fan, it's worth a watch. <br /> <br /> <b>Candyman</b> (1992), based on one of Clive Barker's novellas, about an urban legend come to life in Chicago's notorious Cabrini-Green housing projects. If you've never seen it, I recommend it. Tony Todd is, IMO, an underrated actor, and there's a lot to mine here for WoD ideas, be it doing Chicago by Night in the late 80s and early 90s, the idea of a malevolent Chimera trying to make itself &quot;real&quot; in Changeling, the impact of Wraith hauntings on a community, or a concept for a certain type of Arcanum witch hunter. <br /> <br /> <b>Rosemary's Baby</b> (1968), a low-key horror classic involving secret Satanic cults. <br /> <br /> <b>The Princess and The Frog</b> (2009), one of the last things Disney did using traditional animation, set in New Orleans with a voodoo bokor voiced by Keith David for the villain.<br /> <br /> <b>The 9th Precinct</b> (2019), a rather odd Taiwanese film involving a secret police branch that deals with ghosts and hauntings. Rather fun, and an interesting source for the forthcoming WoD: Ghosthunters as well as Year of the Lotus/Middle Kingdom paranormal investigators. <br /> <br /> <b>He Never Died</b> (2015), with aging punk icon Henry Rollins starting as a cursed immortal totally divorced from humanity forced into a relationship with a now grown daughter he didn't know he had. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T15:39:12-07:00","id":1376018,"title":"","content":"Locke and Key, October Faction, The Order, Always a Witch, Jinn, Spectrez, Dark, Hemlock Grove,Requiem, Glitch, Chilling Adventures of Sabrina, Ghoul, Santa Clarita Diet, iZombie, Penny Dreadful, Crazyhead.<br /> <br /> That should get you started. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T16:21:53-07:00","id":1376023,"title":"","content":"Just watched Annhilation and I liked it, but then I like the kinda wierd WTF movies. The landscapes though as said were phenomenal and very Middle Umbra for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T20:56:39-07:00","id":1376064,"title":"","content":"I just watched <i>The Ritual</i> last night, and highly recommend it. I think I'd peg it as most echoing the vibe I felt from early Werewolf games, though I suppose it could easily bee seen in light of Changeling too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T08:14:42-07:00","id":1376262,"title":"","content":"These are some movies that resonate with me as either inspired by White Wolfs RPGs or movies that White Wolf took inspiration from.<br /> <br /> <b>The Crow</b> - As Gothic punk a movie as I can possibly thing of. <br /> <br /> <b>The Freightners</b> - A comedic movie but one that has a lot of good inspiration for a Wraith game or another game featuring wraiths.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctor Strange</b> - Never played Mage but from what Ive read of it you could do worse for a movie that deals with themes of the game.<br /> <br /> <b>Underworld</b> - Like it or not the blatant WoD rip off did a good job of making an entertaining vampire v werewolf action movie and has the right gothic motif.<br /> <br /> <b>Skinwalkers</b> - Maybe a B movie but one that succeeds in many ways in creating a tense thriller featuring werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T13:57:07-07:00","id":1376306,"title":"","content":"If we're gonna mention <b>The Frighteners</b> and <b>The Crow</b>, lemme toss <b>The Prophecy </b>on to that pile. A Classic for the Demon The Fallen players amongst us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T14:58:26-07:00","id":1376314,"title":"","content":"A few things currently streaming on HULU.<br /> <br /> <b>Pet Semitary</b> (2019), the recent remake. I've always considered this a really good WoD story, as it involves the idea of cursed ground and evil spirits. <br /> <br /> <b>The Cabin in the Woods</b> (2011), because I recently rewatched this with the idea that this is how PENTEX's Slaughterhouse Video currently makes its horror films. <br /> <br /> <b>The French Connection</b> (1971), a classic about cops vs heroin smugglers in NYC.<br /> <br /> <b>Odd Thomas</b> (2014), based on the first book in a series by Dean Koontz, about a medium/psychic who can see malevolent spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>The Possession</b> (2012), about a young girl possessed by a Jewish spectre known as a dybbuk. <br /> <br /> <b>Mimic</b> (1997), an experiment resulting in giant bugs in the city's underground subways. <br /> <br /> <b>Pi</b> (1998), a rather surreal bit about a mathematician who ends up being pursued by a Wall Street conspiracy and Jewish numerologists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T15:30:33-07:00","id":1376320,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Kindred The Embraced</i></b>. At one time, I might have said that it wasn't a good representation of the WoD, because it was too different from the actual WoD (and V:tM) as written, in addition to having been so melodramatic and self-serious despite being very campy, that it came off like a farce. I actually told a friend once that it was V:tM only by virtue of having been (a) about vampires, and (b) having licensed the use of certain proper nouns.<br /> <br /> Having said that, and given recent developments in the direction taken by the actual tabletop game (i.e., what constitutes being &quot;authentic&quot; to V:tM as of late)... I have to admit that history appears to have acquitted <i>Kindred the Embraced</i>. It was clearly just <u>way</u> ahead of its time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 03-23-2020, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T17:18:21-07:00","id":1376628,"title":"","content":"Some more stuff on Amazon Prime video.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon City Shinjuku</b> (1988), a classic anime film that was an influence on certain parts of KotE.<br /> <br /> <b>Sleepy Hollow</b> (1999), one of those fun &quot;Goth 90s&quot; films, back before Tim Burton and Johnny Depp became hollow parodies of themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Childs Play</b> (1988), a classic slasher film and one of the better ones from the post-Nightmare on Elm Street supernatural slasher period.<br /> <br /> <b>Dog Soldiers</b> (2002), one of the better werewolf films.<br /> <br /> <b>Teen Wolf</b> (2011+), the dark reimagining that aired on MTV.<br /> <br /> <b>Mr. Robot</b> (2015+)<br /> <br /> <b>Deadwood</b> (2004 - 2006)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T00:47:40-07:00","id":1379189,"title":"","content":"Finished watching <b>Book of Blood</b> on Amazon Prime tonight. It's based on a short story by Clive Barker from his debut anthology Books of Blood, and I would put it up there with the original Hellraiser and Candyman films. I highly recommend it if you like ghost stories, are a Wraith fan, or are looking forward to the forthcoming WoD Ghosthunters book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:37:26-07:00","id":1379300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1376262#post1376262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are some movies that resonate with me as either inspired by White Wolfs RPGs or movies that White Wolf took inspiration from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember Richard Dansky jokingly referring to <b>The Frighteners</b> as <b>Wraith: The Movie</b> at a mid-90s GenCon panel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T18:17:51-07:00","id":1379366,"title":"","content":"Castlevania series on Netflix is fantastic for Dark Ages WoD.<br /> <br /> The third season was amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T21:26:19-07:00","id":1379402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1379366#post1379366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castlevania series on Netflix is fantastic for Dark Ages WoD.<br /> <br /> The third season was amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to get around to watching that. The most recent show I binge watched on Netflix was a Korean show called <b>Black</b>, which I enjoyed quite a bit. If you like Wraith, especially the Mediums aspect, it's very interesting. It also manages to tie a whole bunch of various mysteries and events into a single coherent plot, including events that suddenly make sense or change your perspective when reseen from a different character's POV. My only complaint was that it didn't quite stick the landing in the final episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T11:36:16-07:00","id":1385435,"title":"","content":"It's arguably more Mage the Awakening, but &quot;The Case Files of El-Melloi II&quot; is available on Crunchyroll and is great Mage politics/investigation inspiration, especially for an Order of Hermes focused chronicle. It is a spin-off from the Fate/stay night franchise (and specifically acts as a sequel to Fate/zero, the F/sn prequel anime which is on Cruncyroll and dubbed on Netflix and is really good in its own right), and follows a mage who is forced to play politics and try to work of a debt (both literal and one he feels he owes someone). There's also a light novel series based on it and at least part of it has been adapted into manga form, but if you just want to watch, the anime is there. It doesn't deal with the &quot;reality war&quot; or Paradox as much, but definitely looks at politics between people and groups that are at least somewhat detached from humanity - even the main character, himself somewhat more humane than his colleagues and dismissive of tradition - shows a side at times that reflects how mage culture is detached from human culture<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I can't say that the Fate animes are great inspiration for World of Darkness games - there are elements and episodes that certainly are great, but the Servant on Servant battles are more reflected of Scion or Exalted. That said, of all the anime series, Fate/zero does look somewhat at politics and focuses more on the Masquerade-esque concept that is supposed to hide the Magic world and the Grail War specifically, and has a few episodes that really feel WoDdy to me (it also is a bit more crossover-esque, since at least two of the Masters are really more akin to hunters of some variety than mages, which is reflected in how they fight and think).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T16:07:29-07:00","id":1385474,"title":"","content":"The Ninth Gate is on Amazon Prime. An reclusive occultist sends Johnny Depp on a harrowing search for a working copy of his defective eldritch tome, failing to realize that the search itself is the real magical initiation. The movie lends itself to a reading as a story about a Mage's Awakening, in addition to being a parable about the folly of using books as a substitute for lived experience instead of as a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-03-2020, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:08:21-07:00","id":1385494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1385474#post1385474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ninth Gate is on Amazon Prime. An reclusive occultist sends Johnny Depp on a harrowing search for a working copy of his defective eldritch tome, failing to realize that the search itself is the real magical initiation. The movie lends itself to a reading as a story about a Mage's Awakening, in addition to being a parable about the folly of using books as a substitute for lived experience instead of as a supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really enjoy that film, even if it is by Roman Polanski, and is usually one of the first things I point to if asked about the Arcanum. I'll also note it's an adaption of a novel by Spanish author Arturo Perez-Reverte called <i>The Club Dumas</i>. An unrelated novel, <i>The Flanders Panel</i>, is also good Arcanum stuff, though I've never seen the 1994 film adaption <i>Uncovered</i>. His Captain Alatriste novels - which he initially started writing to encourage his teenaged daughter's study of history - are good Sorcerers' Crusade reading, and his novel <i>The Fencing Master</i> has inspired more than a few of my Hermetic characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T18:19:18-07:00","id":1385699,"title":"","content":"Oi, been a while fellers. but lets see..<br /> <br /> <b>MirrorMask</b> : by Dave Mckean for changeling reasons<br /> <br /> <b>Coraline</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Mothman Prophecies<br /> <br /> Se7en<br /> <br /> Fight Club<br /> <br /> The Haunting of Hill House<br /> <br /> The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo<br /> <br /> Alan Moore's Jimmy's End.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:46:52-07:00","id":1387557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1376064#post1376064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just watched <i>The Ritual</i> last night, and highly recommend it. I think I'd peg it as most echoing the vibe I felt from early Werewolf games, though I suppose it could easily bee seen in light of Changeling too.</div> </div> </div> </div>could also be some of the revenant bloodlines in found in the aplachian mountain range","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:49:43-07:00","id":1388637,"title":"","content":"I would add also an old (1993) HBO movie once available on video tapes. With Mario van Peebles, Bruce Payne and Patsy Kensit. Unfortunately I don't know where to find it (in Poland I found it in CDA). It's called &quot;Full Eclipse&quot; and it's the best film about werewolves. <br /> <br /> Of course one would say that &quot;Wolf&quot; with Nicholson, Pfeiffer and Spade is better.<br /> <br /> Of other films I would reccomend are:<br /> &quot;The Hunger&quot; - with Catherine Deneuve, David Bowie and Susan Sarandon. About aging. Cause time is a factor, even for vampires.<br /> &quot;The Wolfen&quot; - based on the novel of the same man who wrote The Hunger it's a police story and it's second best werewolf movie I know. It was even mentioned in &quot;Under A Blood Red Moon&quot; (not as a quote, NPCs watched it). Starring Albert Finney. <br /> &quot;The Company of Wolves&quot; - an old movie by Neil Jordan. A variation about Little Red Riding Hood. Starring Sarah Patterson, Angela Lansbury, Stephen Rea and David Warner.<br /> &quot;Dog Soldiers&quot; - what would happen if SAS make their training grounds near the caern. Starring Sean Pertwee and Kevin McKidd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-17-2020, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:29:40-07:00","id":1389965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1376306#post1376306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're gonna mention <b>The Frighteners</b> and <b>The Crow</b>, lemme toss <b>The Prophecy </b>on to that pile. A Classic for the Demon The Fallen players amongst us.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Fallen </b>with Denzel Washington also works as a Demon the Fallen movie. Beyond the simple naming similarity it has a lot of themes and plot ideas that might inspire a Demon campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:22:03-07:00","id":1390024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1375873-wod-stuff-to-watch-while-home?p=1388637#post1388637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of other films I would reccomend are:<br /> &quot;The Hunger&quot; - with Catherine Deneuve, David Bowie and Susan Sarandon. About aging. Cause time is a factor, even for vampires.<br /> &quot;The Wolfen&quot; - based on the novel of the same man who wrote The Hunger it's a police story and it's second best werewolf movie I know. It was even mentioned in &quot;Under A Blood Red Moon&quot; (not as a quote, NPCs watched it). Starring Albert Finney.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whitley Striber wrote a number of pretty good horror novels back in the 70s and early 80s. Then he got abducted by aliens and started writing almost exclusively about that for the next twenty years. <br /> <br /> An interesting compare &amp; contrast exercise is to watch The Hunger and Wolfen with the idea that they take place in the same world and are what vampires and werewolves are like in that universe. Then do the same with John Landis's An American Werewolf in London and Innocent Blood. (I also find it amusing to consider that the original Terminator and Near Dark also take place in the same world.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:21:02-07:00","id":1390061,"title":"","content":"There are a few series I have been watching lately have that a WoD vibe to them:<br /> <br /> <i>Penny Dreadful<br /> <br /> True Detective<br /> <br /> Carniv\u00e0le<br /> <br /> Carvinval Row</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T17:43:30-07:00","id":1390882,"title":"","content":"Not a &quot;too watch,&quot; but some podcasts are solid.<br /> <br /> <i>White Vault </i>has a very Wod, or CoD, feel to it.<br /> <br /> Edited to add:<br /> <i>Limetown<br /> Alice isn't Dead<br /> No Sleep</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-23-2020, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T14:25:42-07:00","id":1391046,"title":"","content":"Folks have probably already heard of it, but if we're adding podcasts then 'Welcome to Night Vale' has a very Cod-Twilight Zone kinda feel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:09:58-07:00","id":1391437,"title":"","content":"<b>The World of Darkness </b>documentary on Amazon or Youtube.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1UMf8SgSH5A\" data-code=\"1UMf8SgSH5A\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1UMf8SgSH5A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:35:06-07:00","id":1393187,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend the television show, Grimm, for something with a bit of a Changeling vibe. The episodes, especially the earliest ones, are all themed around folklore and dark fairy tales (as murders, investigated by the police), and involve a group of people who have hidden supernatural traits that form the basis of a complex society that exists entirely unperceived by ordinary humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:15:18-07:00","id":1411967,"title":"","content":"From Amazon Prime, I watched <b>Dark Was the Night</b>, a 2014 film about ... something ... that gets stirred up when logging starts in a previously undeveloped forest. Said something begins to prowl about the nearby town. I think it's meant to be set in upstate New York, but it never really specifies. It's a slow burn film, more interested in atmosphere and suspense than in kills and gore. And in that sense it's really effective. At least up until about the last 10 or 15 minutes, when you actually start to see the creature instead of just having it hinted at. (I'll be honest, what I was picturing in my head was better than the CGI their budget could afford, and I think it would've benefitted greatly from going with almost all old school practical effects instead.) But still, it's very much worth a watch, especially if you're a Werewolf fan.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, dancing bats:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/v2vp9hl7W98\" data-code=\"v2vp9hl7W98\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v2vp9hl7W98/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:42:40-07:00","id":1411971,"title":"","content":"I should recommend Ancient Magnus bride a beautiful story about a Kinan and the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 09-06-2020, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://